// The source of the moves of `npc_gnu_ton`: the scholar GNU-ton as a fighter.
// The game loads this file through the content pack (`assets/pack.ron`); edit it here.
// Its grab boxes are stated for its standing height (65.0), not for the 48 of a
// row that states none: a grab is the reach of the body, so it grows with the body.
//
// DESIGN NOTES.
//
// A light, fast FENCER with two tools. The QUILL is long and thin: it wins by
// reach and by speed, it does little, and it does not end a stock. The BOOK is
// short and slow: it is what ends one (the back air, the back throw). He is
// light: what hits him sends him far.
//
// His SMASH ATTACKS are not his own. He opens the line of a portal, and the
// fist of his giant comes out of it (the effects `gnu_fist_*` of
// `gnu_ton_vfx`; the hit volume is the fist's). They are of this stage only:
// in his boss fight the giant is under him, and the same moves are a blow of
// his book (`bosses/gnu_ton/duel.rs`).
//
// His specials are his laws. Neutral: Opticks (a flash, the same launch at each
// percent). Side: a fluxion (he goes forward through you). Up: levity (a save,
// not a flight). Down: the Third Law (a counter; the reaction is a strike).
// Down in the air: universal gravitation (he comes down as the apple did).
//
// FIRST CUT, 2026-10-11. The table was derived from the patent clerk's (for
// its format: the grab kit, the counter, the gates), with each move's times,
// damage, launch and reach set for this body. The numbers are a start for
// play, not a result of it. His own effects (ink, apples) are not made: each
// move draws the common slash.
